    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d800">

                <pb facs="0815" n="697" xml:id="pg697"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/6341: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chargé in
                        Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hanna</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-06-14T16:00:00-04:00">June 14, 1929—4
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>89. Legation’s 160, June 12, noon;<anchor n="1" xml:id="d800-f1"/> 162, June 13,
                    noon: and 164, June 13, 5 p.m. The Department regards with interest the proposal
                    to construct roads in the bandit areas but before authorizing you to discuss the
                    subject with the Nicaraguan Government desires to receive from you a report
                    describing the roads it is contemplated to build, the number of persons who
                    would be employed, and related features. In this connection you are advised that
                    it is the Department’s opinion that any road construction undertaken should
                    contemplate the permanent needs and economic advancement of the Republic as well
                    as immediate military advantage.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Clark</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
